<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8' standalone='yes'?>
<catalogue xmlns="http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/catalogueSchema" library="false" id="bef6-c43d-cca8-c5a7" name="Imperial Guard (4E)" gameSystemId="sys-b41a-8226-286b-0dea" gameSystemRevision="5" revision="1" authorName="Community submission" battleScribeVersion="2.03" type="catalogue" publicationId="8c36-25a5-bb95-6fec">
  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Leadership" id="acf5-5f99-a91b-b647" hidden="false">
      <description>Any Imperial Guard unit within 12" of an Officer may use that Officer’s Leadership for Morale and Leadership tests, so long as the Officer is not in close combat, falling back, or pinned.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Advisors" id="e86f-be37-518b-a37c" hidden="false">
      <description>Commissars, Priests and Sanctioned Psykers are Advisors. For each Advisor type, the first must be allocated to the Command HQ; subsequent Advisors of that type are allocated to Platoon HQs. After all Command and Platoon HQs have one of that Advisor type, remaining Advisors may be assigned individually to Infantry Squads, Armoured Fist Squads or Storm Trooper Squads. Unattached Advisors may not be used.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Infiltrators" id="966b-d155-a0f3-14c3" hidden="false">
      <description>May use the Infiltrators rule if the mission permits.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Deep Strike" id="b6c2-193c-890a-191e" hidden="false">
      <description>May use the Deep Strike rule if the mission permits.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Remnants" id="ec95-fe78-a2d2-b0ef" hidden="false">
      <description>A Platoon with at least four full Infantry Squads may include one Remnants squad. It contains a Sergeant and 4–8 Guardsmen. It may not include a heavy weapon team but may use the other Infantry Squad options.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Scouts (Sentinel)" id="7f77-7823-0537-788a" hidden="false">
      <description>Sentinels may deploy at the start of a battle even where they could not normally be deployed. After both sides have deployed, Sentinels may make a free normal move before rolling for first turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Inferno Cannon" id="c24e-0448-7ce7-c029" hidden="false">
      <description>Designate a target and place the flamer template so that it is at least partially over as many models as possible; the whole template must be within 24" and line of sight. Roll to hit once using the Hellhound’s BS. If it hits, every model partially or wholly under the template is hit; if it misses, each covered model is hit on a 4+.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Hunting Lance" id="a823-1896-1be3-733f" hidden="false">
      <description>Automatically used in the first close combat fought by the Rough Rider. On the charge it gives +2 Strength and +1 Initiative and ignores Armour Saves. It cannot be used again after that combat.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Fleet of Hoof" id="a746-9a99-f3eb-6593" hidden="false">
      <description>If the unit is not going to shoot in the Shooting phase, roll a D6; the unit may move that distance in the Shooting phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ogryn-proof" id="4b83-54b4-cecb-d7ea" hidden="false">
      <description>The ripper gun gives +1 Strength to the Ogryn when used in close combat.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="It’s Dark in Dere!" id="d4c9-8584-6626-5fcb" hidden="false">
      <description>An Ogryn unit will only embark in a Chimera if an Officer or Commissar is within 12" of at least one model when it embarks. Ogryns may start mounted without this requirement and may disembark freely. A unit led by a Bone’ead ignores this rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Bulky" id="28b6-175c-a76f-3d5d" hidden="false">
      <description>Each Ogryn takes up two transport spaces.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Go to Ground" id="6753-2a2f-ffb1-e931" hidden="false">
      <description>Ratlings in cover add +1 to their Cover save. If required to take a Morale test for 25% shooting casualties while in cover, they may choose to be Pinned instead of taking the test.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Blessing of the Machine-God" id="90e0-4222-1193-7a62" hidden="false">
      <description>A Techpriest Enginseer that starts the turn in contact with an immobilised vehicle or one with a Weapon Destroyed result may attempt a repair. The chosen defect is repaired on a 6+, with +1 to the roll for each Technical Servitor accompanying him.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Fire Points (Chimera)" id="5558-eadf-d412-f146" hidden="false">
      <description>Up to six passengers may use the Chimera’s hull lasguns to fire at one target. One model may fire from the top hatch; doing so makes the Chimera count as open-topped for resolving enemy shooting attacks until the next turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Amphibious" id="4965-327c-abe7-6ef0" hidden="false">
      <description>A Chimera treats water features as clear terrain when moving.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Indirect Fire" id="cbb4-2c17-32bb-0249" hidden="false">
      <description>A Basilisk upgraded for indirect fire may fire the Earthshaker at targets it cannot draw line of sight to. Fired this way it is a barrage (Guess range) weapon with minimum range 36" and maximum range 240".</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Harsh Discipline" id="ac40-1afe-3782-c684" hidden="false">
      <description>While Colonel Schaeffer is alive, all Last Chancer sub-units automatically pass Morale, Leadership and Pinning tests they are required to make.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Last Chancers — Sub-units" id="6231-fdc0-b43f-d124" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of the game the Last Chancers may be split into up to five sub-units, each with as few as one model. Models in the same heavy weapon team must remain in the same sub-unit and no sub-unit may contain more than one demolition charge.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Doctrine System" id="c3f3-bfd9-8eee-daf6" hidden="false">
      <description>Using Regimental Doctrines is optional. A regiment using Doctrines has five Doctrine points. Each selected Doctrine uses one point unless otherwise stated. Restricted Troop types are unavailable unless their Restricted Troops Doctrine is selected. Some famous regiments list more than five Doctrines; those published examples represent their established organisations.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Guard Infantry" id="7cf2-ffa2-d390-f43d" hidden="false">
      <description>For Doctrine purposes, Guard Infantry includes Command Squads with their Officers and Advisors, Anti-tank Support Squads, Fire Support Squads, Special Weapons Support Squads, Mortar Support Squads, Hardened Veterans, normal Infantry Platoon squads and Armoured Fist Squads.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
